course: dictionary
lesson: 9452
title: Stanzas in poems
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A poem is often written in groups of lines. Each group is called a stanza. «A stanza is a group of lines in a poem, like a paragraph in a story.»
explain: Look for the space between the groups. One stanza ends, the space comes, and the next stanza starts. A stanza is also called a verse.
explain: Counting stanzas helps you see how a poem is built. Poets choose each stanza carefully, because each one can show a new idea or feeling.
fact: A stanza is a group of lines in a poem.
fact: Stanzas are separated by a space, like paragraphs in a story.
fact: A stanza is also called a verse.
fact: A couplet has 2 lines, a tercet has 3 lines and a quatrain has 4 lines.
fact: In a song, the repeated part is called the chorus.
exercise: «A stanza is a group of lines in a poem, like a paragraph in a story.» What is a stanza? | The page number of a story | A single word in a poem | *A group of lines in a poem | A type of picture book
exercise: A group of 4 lines in a poem is called what? | A couplet | *A quatrain | A chorus | A tercet
exercise: In a song, the part that repeats is called what? | The title | A couplet | A stanza | *The chorus
test: A stanza is also called what? | A title | A chapter | *A verse | A sentence
test: How many lines does a couplet have? | Three | Four | One | *Two
exam: Ellie's poem has four lines, then a space, then three more lines. How many stanzas does it have? | Three | Seven | One | *Two
